\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Wherewith, O God, shall I draw near,
\par And bow myself before Thy face?
\par How in Thy purer eyes appear?
\par What shall I bring to gain Thy grace?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Who'er to Thee themselves approve
\par Must take the path Thy Word hath showed,
\par Justice pursue, and mercy love,
\par And humbly walk by faith with God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. But though my life henceforth be Thine,
\par Present for past can ne'er atone:
\par Though I to Thee the whole resign,
\par I only give Thee back Thine own.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. What have I then wherein to trust?
\par I nothing have, I nothing am;
\par Excluded is my every boast,
\par My glory swallowed up in shame.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Guilty I stand before Thy face,
\par On me I feel Thy wrath abide;
\par 'Tis just the sentence should take place;
\par 'Tis just- but O Thy Son hath died!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Jesus, the Lamb of God, hath bled,
\par He bore our sins upon the tree;
\par Beneath our curse He bowed His head,
\par 'Tis finished! He hath died for me!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. See where before the throne He stands,
\par And pours the all-prevailing prayer,
\par Points to His side, and lifts His hands,
\par And shows that I am graven there.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. He ever lives for me to pray;
\par He prays that I with Him may reign;
\par Amen to what my Lord doth say!
\par Jesus, Thou canst not pray in vain.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

